"""Publish only authored test receipts; never process real-session logs."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,shutil,re
ROOT=Path(__file__).parent;OUT=ROOT/'static';DEST=OUT/'tools-audit-data';DEST.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
def read(name):
 p=ROOT/'logs'/name
 return json.loads(p.read_text()) if p.exists() else {}
browser=read('tools-browser-20261114.json');model=read('tools-live-20261114.json');follow=read('tool-followups-live-20261114.json');mic=read('tools-microphone-20261114.json')
literal=read('tools-literal-model-20261114.json');smoke=read('tools-final-smoke-20261114.json')
for name in ('tools-browser-20261114.json','tools-live-20261114.json','tool-followups-live-20261114.json','tools-microphone-20261114.json','tools-literal-model-20261114.json','tools-final-smoke-20261114.json'):
 p=ROOT/'logs'/name
 if p.exists():shutil.copy2(p,DEST/name)
def e(x):return html.escape(str(x))
def rows(cases):return ''.join('<tr><td>'+e(x.get('request',''))+'</td><td>'+('Passed' if x.get('passed') else 'Failed / incomplete')+'</td><td>'+e(x.get('error',''))+'</td></tr>' for x in cases)
checks=''.join(f'<tr><td>{"Serial verified" if x.get("serial") else "Parallel verified" if x["enabled"] else "Raw (verification off)"}</td><td>{x["metrics"].get("tts_first_audio_ms","—")}</td><td>{x["metrics"].get("llm_first_sentence_ms","—")}</td><td>{x["metrics"].get("first_audio_ms","—")}</td></tr>' for x in browser.get('checks',[]))
unit=(ROOT/'logs/tools-audit-unit-final.log').read_text() if (ROOT/'logs/tools-audit-unit-final.log').exists() else ''
unit_result=re.search(r'(\d+ passed[^\n]*)',unit)
body=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Robby · tools and latency audit</title><style>body{{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 22px;color:#243e50;background:#fffdf9}}h1{{line-height:1.2}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:20px 0}}td,th{{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #d8e0e6;padding:10px;vertical-align:top}}.scroll{{overflow:auto}}.card{{background:#e9f3ef;padding:18px;border-radius:14px}}a{{color:#216a76}}code{{overflow-wrap:anywhere}}</style>
<a href="/desk-robot/">← Live Robby</a><h1>Robby: reliable tool routing &amp; visible latency choices</h1><p>Implementation audit · 14 November 2026 · RTX 3090 · Qwen 27B / Cerebras · Humaneness Small RL.</p>
<div class="card"><strong>Real browser integration:</strong> {e(browser.get('passed','not run'))}. {len(browser.get('turns',[]))} authored requests, real generated PCM, actual renderer frames and actual returned source links. <strong>Regression contracts:</strong> {e(unit_result[1] if unit_result else 'pending')}. <strong>Synthetic microphone tier:</strong> {e(mic.get('passed','pending'))}.</div>
<h2>What changed</h2><p>Both directors share a capability catalogue. Wake-address variants, serious faces, puppy eyes, cheek puffing and blinking have explicit mappings. Model-selected tools can escalate from the sentence-streaming path, including calls emitted after introductory text. A spoken promise is not used as proof that a tool ran. The same validators enforce bounded visual actions and authorized session rules.</p>
<p>Implicit research requests use the recent subject. News headline requests no longer accidentally filter for the literal words “aktuelle Schlagzeilen”. General web lookup returns actual OpenRouter/Exa source annotations and extracts; it uses the configured API account and incurs search/model charges. No CAPTCHA bypass or unrestricted browser is exposed.</p>
<h2>Verification choices: actual browser observations</h2><p>Same authored phrase, one live turn per setting. These are smoke-test observations, not a statistically controlled speed benchmark; model output, warm-up and provider scheduling can differ. First PCM is server-side, before the browser's playback reserve.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>TTS → first PCM, ms</th><th>LLM → first sentence, ms</th><th>Request → first PCM, ms</th></tr>{checks}</table></div>
<p>The second input recognizer can be disabled independently; native Nemotron and the speech-pause guard remain. The generated-speech check can be disabled for earlier raw playback, at the cost of exposing wrong words and unwanted leading/trailing audio. Serial output checking is an optional comparison. Speaker admission and stop handling are unaffected.</p>
<h2>HTTPS end-to-end cases</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Request</th><th>Result</th><th>Failure detail</th></tr>{rows(browser.get('turns',[]))}</table></div>
<p>Rendered catalogue: {len(browser.get('catalogue',{}).get('poses',[]))} emotions; {browser.get('catalogue',{}).get('uniquePoses','—')} distinct authored control patterns; {len(browser.get('catalogue',{}).get('faces',[]))} grimace variants. This tests authored pose differences, not human perceptual recognition of all emotion labels. Mobile guide: {e(browser.get('guide',{}))}.</p>
<h2>Follow-up interpretation and rule tools</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Request</th><th>Result</th><th>Failure detail</th></tr>{rows(follow.get('cases',[]))}</table></div><p>Rule tests use an isolated synthetic rule book, never a visitor's live session. They test rule installation/clearing; they do not establish real-room interruption accuracy in noise.</p>
<h2>Microphone path</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Authored synthetic utterance</th><th>Result</th><th>Failure detail</th></tr>{rows(mic.get('turns',[]))}</table></div><p>{e(mic.get('error',''))} Chrome's fake microphone carries generated Idris speech into the real ASR pipeline. This is not a physical microphone or multi-person TV/background-noise evaluation.</p>
<h2>Service and test limitations</h2><p>The initial model suite exposed missing synonyms, a generic-news-query bug and Cerebras rejecting the search plugin's extra system message. Those were corrected. The burst of API tests also hit HTTP 429 rate limits; those failures are retained rather than relabeled as passes. Provider/API outages remain possible. Existing output-ASR retries can also add latency if a take contains incorrect words. Browser reduced-motion and disabled-action preferences still suppress motion.</p>
<p>An extra final literal-speech browser probe could not acquire the pilot's single conversation slot while a live conversation was active; it is recorded as incomplete, not passed. The running conversation was not interrupted. The equivalent real-model/pipeline test with TTS disabled passed: {e(literal.get('passed','not run'))}. This extra probe is separate from the completed ten-turn HTTPS suite and two microphone cases above. The pilot currently accepts one conversation session at a time.</p>
<p>In a negative German test, native Nemotron misheard “Hey Robby” as “Hey Hobby”, and the wake gate correctly ignored it. Disabling the second recognizer therefore does not preserve German wake-word reliability. A separate English “somer salt” split-word failure was fixed by adding the recognized spelling to the somersault mapping. Microphone, gaze, memory, voice isolation and the podcast service were preserved; this task did not retrain or recalibrate multi-speaker recognition. The existing TTS and podcast processes and Cloudflare tunnel were not restarted. Only the Robby application was restarted to deploy code.</p>
<h2>Reproduce and inspect</h2><p>Source scripts: <code>validate_tools_live.py</code>, <code>validate_tool_followups_live.py</code>, <code>browser_tools_audit.py</code>, <code>browser_tools_microphone.py</code>, <code>test_tool_capabilities.py</code>. Operator instructions and full rationale: <code>TOOLS_AND_LATENCY_GUIDE.md</code> and <code>VOICE_ASSISTANT_TEST_PROTOCOL.md</code>.</p><ul>
{''.join(f'<li><a href="/static/tools-audit-data/{e(p.name)}">{e(p.name)}</a></li>' for p in sorted(DEST.glob('*.json')))}
</ul><p><a href="/static/tool-catalogue.json">Actual capability schemas</a> · <a href="/desk-robot/#system-guide">Three architecture diagrams</a> · <a href="/static/parallel-tts-verification.html">Earlier controlled verification study</a></p></html>'''
# Empty dict expressions are deliberately kept simple outside the HTML template.
(OUT/'tools-audit.html').write_text(body)
